extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada, China agree to ease tariffs amid trade rows with US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87ca89b380c05f62494724f433c9fb39f7bda8fb6ce305bf741d1ed9d4ab3cc6</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T07:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-china-agree-to-ease-tariffs-amid-trade-rows-with-us/a-79964912--5804d9c43235.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-china-agree-to-ease-tariffs-amid-trade-rows-with-us/a-79964912?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Canadian and Chinese leaders have vowed closer cooperation as both nations seek to reduce reliance on the US. Canada's government said it had agreed to further reduce tariffs on a range of products.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Modi proposes e-visas for ASEAN tourists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01ca02d0fe1c2fae071edb6215a5bc440a9ec3b1f3976c78c0bf3b39ab9bfb6c</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-proposes-e-visas-for-asean-tourists/live-79964913--bbeaefe8a8e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-proposes-e-visas-for-asean-tourists/live-79964913?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking at the ASEAN summit in Manila, Modi said that India's development and ASEAN's prosperity are "deeply interconnected."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mongolian President Khurelsukh to resign amid corruption allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:442521740030e71bcba4cb575be5ce9d1009ea51301b7847c2f2310bf6929190</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mongolian-president-khurelsukh-to-resign-amid-corruption-allegations/a-79964717--8f5d5c920ebb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mongolian-president-khurelsukh-to-resign-amid-corruption-allegations/a-79964717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Khurelsukh has said he will step down over accusations that he profited from a government railway project, but said he had been "falsely accused."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan scrambles jets to counter suspected Russian aircraft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:300aaa97238be15a9a6c923d4fb76f15043b1b0850ed20ae3d3f6ccdcf2bcbe0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T03:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-scrambles-jets-to-counter-suspected-russian-aircraft/a-79964537--8dcebae15e8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-scrambles-jets-to-counter-suspected-russian-aircraft/a-79964537?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan said it lodged a "very stern protest" with Moscow after two suspected Russian aircraft violated Japanese airspace.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Former leader Khan pleads for medical care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eefcbcd9d1a0e6c5144a3416b2173ae3c0a79b27d3690d04c918985203137ccb</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T19:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-former-leader-khan-pleads-for-medical-care/a-79961718--6ad62e15aecb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-former-leader-khan-pleads-for-medical-care/a-79961718?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Imran Khan appealed to judges to be treated "before it's too late." His wife was also included in the request.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia scandal: China's chips dilemma, US rivalry shape AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca7202ddb1b000427c46e111ff3385c507e663b9bafc24bbdb84daf3cd20cf70</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-scandal-china-s-chips-dilemma-us-rivalry-shape-ai-race/a-79961766--39b6798086ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-scandal-china-s-chips-dilemma-us-rivalry-shape-ai-race/a-79961766?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The controversy over Nvidia's former CEO Jensen Huang and an alleged affair with a suspected spy has exposed the intensifying AI rivalry between the US and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f23084f70e15045c38c90d9620f3e48e3b151aa8b24fbffc3df3dd43fe5d921</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China faces Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2b14490249e0b6885f377f21b3b84b934bb41c3bcf7a4a1c35fe5b5326d5a5</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--86131bd0e961.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Russia, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5bed9d39a641447d13bd6b033b870dbee08c7a480dd54ce67069e74d3496d00</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753--1c825a485886.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89cacca9b340244bac27a114b3ab5b8734187b6eaa1891bc6dfae64d2e088aee</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
